# OCR roadmap (3 Sep 2026)

Read `docs/OCR-ROADMAP.md` before touching `training/` or `data/ocr/`. Update its status board when a step lands.

**Closed:** fine-tuning on EasyOCR-labelled Mapillary crops — passes 14–19, five sets, no gain. Do not relaunch pass-8 through pass-19. Do not relabel the 20,240 photographs and retry; it is still the model labelling its own training data. The photographs stay (`afaksrmeli/lilly-mapillary-photos`, Mac `data/ocr/real-photos/mapillary/`); lists in `data/ocr/mapillary-train/gt.txt` (915) and `data/ocr/mapillary-train-clean/gt.txt` (713) are records, not train sets.

**Next, in order:** (1) PaddleOCR PP-OCRv5 untrained vs shipped, on the Mac or a Kaggle CPU notebook, bar written in `training/PREREGISTRATION.md` first; (2) `test-v2`: ≥1,500 agreed words over ≥150 Commons photographs, two blind transcribers, split by source photograph, never trained on; (3) detection recall R_d as pre-registered; (4) fine-tuning only with labels from humans or a blind-checked non-EasyOCR vision model, same domain as the test; (5) Cyrillic after 1–3.

**Measurement rules:** only held-out crops compare readers — `labels-human-latin.tsv` is 666/737 training-side. Counts beside percentages, interval beside the delta (132 crops ±8, 25 letters ±19); inside the interval is "no change". Both readers in one process on the same crops, on the GPU that holds the weights. Any reader that writes labels goes through `app.ocr.read_regions`, never a bare `easyocr.Reader`.

Product bar: a folded reading that translates is enough (`kuca` → House). The crop gate letter column is unchanged and can still refuse the run.
